Perspective-faithful body scaling — render bodies at true angular size

Replace fixed 235x-exaggerated body sizes with per-frame perspective-faithful
scaling. Every body now renders at the angular size a human observer would
perceive from the camera's position, with a 3px minimum so distant bodies
remain visible. Close to the Sun it fills the screen; from Earth's distance
it's a small bright disk — matching reality.

Key changes:
- True proportional radii (radiusKm / AU_KM * AU_SCENE) for all bodies
- Per-frame updatePerspectiveScaling() scales meshes, coronas, glows, axes
- Dynamic camera.near and controls.minDistance for close zoom on small bodies
- Navigation viewDist uses true radii instead of exaggerated mesh sizes
- HUD reticle tracks effective (displayed) radius
- Location marker and velocity arrow scale with Earth's perspective factor
- PRINCIPLES.md updated to document the new Tier 2 scale system

This is a large structural change to the scale system. To rollback:
  git revert HEAD
